!! T10 — boot cells in prepareNodeBootOn (open-node-vessel.ts 709-3546)
Frame: the function builds closures in a fixed order, then the shared composer (lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts 106-253) drives the keel: `loadGenesis` (sets `bootstrap`) -> `systemCanon` (sets `activeAtom`, `kahuCanon`, `kahuProtected`, `kahuStandingVessel`) -> `wikiSlot` (sets `slotActiveWikiId`, `activeWikiSource`) -> `openDaemon` (sets many, including `daemonVm`; then `pendingVerbContribution`) -> `wireVerbs` -> `afterDaemon` (stands the sync gates) -> `makePool` (sets `mailbox`, `eventBus`, `vmManager`, `wikiActivation`) -> `afterLive`. That order is imposed by another file; no cell knows it.
Spans: the `let x!` block is lines 1699-1717 in main (line numbers 1697-1795 in the brief). Forward lets total 51 in the function (list below); 6 use definite-assignment `!`.

!!! A. The six `let x!` cells (no initial value: a read before set is undefined, and the type lies)
* `vmManager: VesselIslandPool` (1699). Set: 3372 in makePool (once). Reads: 1803 (`() => vmManager` handed to makeVesselResidency; used by residency onHydrate/onEvict for wiki grains only), 1829 (teardown, cast `as VesselIslandPool | undefined`: the type already admits the lie), 3043 and 3065 (verbs `sync-wiki`, `wiki-act`), 3228 (residency stats), 3322 (mailbox delivery), 3412/3417. HAZARD: `sync-wiki` / `wiki-act` register in wireVerbs, which runs BEFORE makePool; if the daemon island places a main verb in that window the handler throws a bare TypeError on `undefined.placeWikiVerb` (and `wikiActivation.ensureActive` before it). The window is the span of the primary wiki mount; no test pins it. Residency hooks are safe: only grain type "wiki" reads the pool and none is pinned until afterLive.
* `wikiActivation: WikiActivationCap` (1700). Set 3410 (after `new VesselIslandPool`). Reads 3042, 3063, 3208, 3217-3231, 3320. Same pre-makePool verb window as vmManager. The mailbox delivery closure (3319) reads it at drain time; `mailbox` is set (3314) before the pool exists but `wikiActivation` after, so an `onEa` drain firing during the pool constructor would hit undefined; the constructor only builds, mount runs later in core-caps, so safe by construction, again unpinned.
* `mailbox: DurableMailbox` (1701). Set 3314 (first statement of makePool). Reads 1809 (residency `onUndeliverableAlert`, async later) and 3399 (`onEa`). Safe: set before the pool exists.
* `daemonVm: DaemonVmCore` (1710). Set 2579 in openDaemon; `standDaemonVm()` resolves `daemonVmStood` at 2608. Reads: 1083 (rest door waits on `daemonVmStood.then`, safe by promise), 1380/1402/3087/3478/3499/3514 (hand-written `if (!daemonVm) throw|return null` guards, five sites, with the message "the daemon island does not stand yet": the one place the house already refuses by name, by hand), 1706 (`dropFace`, unguarded), 2521 (`lightFace`, unguarded, but reached only after boot), 2743/2958/2965-2966 (inside verb-plane impls, after set), 3029, 3264 and 3296 (afterDaemon), 3304, 3411, 3533 (`daemonVm: () => daemonVm` accessor typed non-null; the Herm dispose calls `p.daemonVm().shutdown()` unguarded, so a boot that failed before openDaemon dereferences undefined in dispose). The `!` plus five `!daemonVm` guards plus the accessor show three conventions for one cell.
* `eventBus: LarEventBusImpl` (1713). Set 3326 in makePool, `start()` then `subscribeWorkerEventsToDaemon()` (3329, reads daemonVm.placeVerb lazily). Reads 1827 (teardown, cast as possibly undefined), 3300, 3397 (worker event path, after set), 3534 accessor. Safe.
* `bootstrap: VesselBootstrap` (1717). Set 1930 in `loadGenesis`. Reads 1833 (`readDaemonDoc`: used by wikiSlot/openDaemon, after), 2156-2178, 2421-2463, 2581-2595, 3253, and 3443-3444 which tolerate undefined with `bootstrap?.daemonUrl ?? ""` (a silent empty default on a cell that is typed non-null). A torn bootstrap throws inside loadGenesis before the set (the intended refusal).

!!! B. Forward lets with a null/noop default (sets and reads; "order hazard" = a read that can run before the set)
Each reads null/noop as an explicit inert or fail-closed state. "Early" means set in straight-line code before the Repo network can carry a peer.
* deviceOfPresenter 785 / set 1441; read 787 -> `{unreadable:"face-device-unbound"}` (closed). Safe.
* sweepSameOperator 801 / set 1470; reads 1276, 1367, 1540 use `?.()`. Safe (skipped sweep before set; refold callbacks may fire before 1470 — a missed sweep, not a leak).
* faceBootTiddlers 804 / set 1905 (loadGenesis); read through `faceViews` gated by `wornFaceProven` (false until 2168). Closed.
* wornFaceProven 807 (false) / set 2168. Closed default.
* kahuCanon 812 ({}) / set 1981; reads 858 (`kahuHandAtWire`), 3335/3336 (disk mirror grant, after). {} reads as no Kahu docs; closed.
* kahuProtected 827 / set 1988 (guard `if (!kahuProtected)`); reads 834, 847, 850-856, 859. FAIL-OPEN until set: see F2. Three `?.`/`??` fallbacks to empty. Candidate for a typed cell whose pre-set state is "withhold everything" (closed), not "withhold nothing".
* kahuStandingVessel 830 ("") / set 1992; read 838 inside `standCarriedKahuStandings`, which first needs `kahuStandings.primary`. Safe. NOTE: set AFTER `recountKahuProtected()` (1991) runs `standCarriedKahuStandings`, so line 1991 can read the empty "" on a carried-home watch if the primary is already set (it is not on first boot: `!kahuStandings.primary` at 1993). A reorder trap on the re-entry path; flag for the brief.
* catalogForViews 863 / set 2035 (first line of openDaemon); read 865 `catalogForViews ? ... : new Set()` closed.
* ownCarriageBoard 872 / set 1570; read 1057 in share verdict (null = no carriage-board refusal; set early, before keel).
* nexusMembershipHolder 883 / set 1281; reads 905, 940, 1215, 1249, 1259, 2254 all `?.`/guarded. Safe.
* representIfMoved 885 / set 2364 (noop) and 2387 (lateDialOnce); reads 1216, 1323 `?.`. Two setters, one cell: single-owner question for the brief.
* antigenRing 955 / set 1198; read 1043. Null denies nobody (documented fail-open default, early set). Candidate for "ban-nobody" being named, not changed.
* selfSlotFedGate 960 / sets 1569, 2265 (`realmPlane.gate`), 2640 (`ring.compose(...)`): three writers widening the same cell in sequence. Read 1042 into `selfSlotShareDecision`, which defends with `?? new DenyAllGate()` (self-slot-share.ts ~129-130). Closed by the decision table.
* siblings 964 / set 2669; siblingGate 965 / set 2642; reads 1036-1040, 1415, 2629, 3529 all `?.`. Closed (sibling ness unproven = not a sibling, then wire verdict).
* realmPlane 969 / set 2217 (guard `!realmPlane && nexusMembership && selfSlotFedGate`); reads 1319, 2216-2266, 3100, 3107, 3531 `?.`/ternary. Safe.
* edgeShadows 974 / set 1416; reads 1062, 1321, 1472, 2636-2642 guarded. Null = sets nobody aside (early set; floor ring variant at 1415).
* nexusMembership 979 / set 1282; reads 1048, 2216-2221. Null = stranger lane (closed).
* houseIslands 996 (`new Set()`) / set 1087 (`islandPeersOf(repo)`); read 1036. Empty = no peer is the house's own, so everything reads as wire (closed).
* resolvedCatalogUrl 1092 / set 1094; gateReadings 1228 ([]) / set 1487; resweepGates 1230 / set 3272 (first afterDaemon); landOwedHostingActs 1309 / set 3280; wornFleetRoot 1342 / set 2090 (read 1352, 3469 guarded); litFace 1344 / set 2472; activeAtom 1345 / sets 1979 (systemCanon) and 2074 (openDaemon): 43 read lines, two writers, the keel's systemCanon runs first and `openDaemon` re-sets; the reads at 1982/1995 use `activeAtom?.key ?? ""` (empty key silently passed to standKahuCanon/watchKahuStanding if the atom did not load: a silent-default candidate).
* rootlessSaid 1376, floorRestSaid 1512, dialStoodDown 1692 (set at 1825 teardown), sameOperatorSweep 1469 (promise), registerRelayPlanes 1513 / set 2440 (read 1543 `?.()`), intentRelay 1551 / sets 1545, 1552 (teardown nulls): TDZ NOTE: `standSyncGates` (defined ~1514) reads `intentRelay` which is declared at 1551, AFTER the arrow; it works only because `standSyncGates` first runs at 3272. Any earlier call is a ReferenceError (temporal dead zone), not a null read.
* nexusDial 1688 / set 2339; read in `lateDialOnce` 2387 and stop at 1825. personaSelves 1718 (memo `??=` at 3447). slotActiveWikiId 1719 ("") / set 2019; activeWikiSource 1720 / set 2018; reads 3042-3062 (`sync-wiki` on "" before wikiSlot runs would target slot ""), 3429. recallFormPalace 1724, recallStructurePalace 1726, recallContent 1741: lazy `??=` memos, no order hazard. pendingVerbContribution 1791 / set 3018, read 3240 which throws by name ("verb plane not composed — wireVerbs ran before openDaemon stashed the contribution"): the one cell that already refuses by name, with a dedicated message and a documented ordering comment. `lightFace` 1702 (noop async default) / set 2517: a silent noop before openDaemon sets it; `standDaemonVm` noop / replaced synchronously in the same function by the Promise executor.
* crossroadsOfferingsHandle 1716 (undefined) / set 2568 (`??=`), reads 2572, 3391 (`?.`: a missing board resolves plugin offerings to none, not an error).

!!! C. Order hazards that survive the read (a read can run before the set)
# `sync-wiki` / `wiki-act` handlers vs `vmManager` + `wikiActivation` between wireVerbs and makePool (bare TypeError, not a named refusal). Window = primary wiki mount.
# `kahuProtected`, `antigenRing`, `edgeShadows`: fail-open nulls guarded only by "gates stand at afterDaemon, one call site". F2.
# `intentRelay` / `standSyncGates` TDZ.
# `bootstrap?.daemonUrl ?? ""` accessors (3443-3444) answer empty before loadGenesis.
# `activeAtom?.key ?? ""` into `standKahuCanon`/`watchKahuStanding`/askSeatDuties: empty-string default instead of refusal at 1982/1995 (askSeatDuties at 1404 refuses by name when atom is absent).
# `kahuStandingVessel` set after the first `standCarriedKahuStandings` call (1991 vs 1992).
# `replayPinsFromDaemonDoc(...)` is `void`ed at 3264 and its own comment demands it finish BEFORE `startSweeper()` (3265): un-awaited, so the "pins replay before the first sweep tick" law holds only because the first tick is an interval away.
# Daemon-vm accessors on result (3533) typed non-null; Herm `dispose` calls `p.daemonVm().shutdown()` unguarded (a boot refused before openDaemon).

!!! D–E. Items 1-9 for T10
# Span: the forward-declared lets listed above, spread over 785-1791 of open-node-vessel.ts; the `!` block 1699-1717.
# Does: holds values that closures defined earlier read lazily once the shared composer fills them in its fixed stage order.
# State: closure-captured only; no env/fs/clock in the cells themselves (the cells hold daemon VM, pool, gates, docs).
# Callers/callees: all in-function; external reads are the result accessors at 3441-3536 (`daemonVm`, `eventBus`, `slotActiveWikiId`, `lightFace`, `daemonDocUrl`, ...). Sets happen in keel (`loadGenesis`, `systemCanon`), `wikiSlot`, `openDaemon`, `afterDaemon`, `makePool`, mostly inside one function each.
# Tests: only through whole boots (8 files import openNodeVessel/openNodeHerm; none pins stage order or a read-before-set). T6 (boot characterization) is the road's cure and T10 waits on it implicitly: do not cut cells without T6's order pins.
# Lift target: stays host-bound orchestration state inside the composer record (T12's orchestration record). The typed cell is a small pure helper (`cell<T>(name)`: `set` once or by declared rule, `get` throws `CellUnset: <name>`); the daemon/pool/bus cells sit behind the shared `VesselOrchestration` stage contract. Cells that feed `selfSlotShareDecision` belong to T11's "one share-inputs cell", not to T10.
# Laws: old shapes burn (the `!`/cast/hand-guard conventions burn together); capability not host; no global now (untouched).
# Risk: (a) SEMANTIC CONFLICT: a refuse-on-read cell turns the intended fail-closed nulls into thrown errors inside the share verdict (`shareConfigOf` async hook). The decision table already defends each null explicitly. Putting a throwing cell there changes closed-by-default into whatever the repo does when a verdict rejects (not measured here). So split cells into two kinds: STAND cells (refuse by name: vmManager, wikiActivation, mailbox, daemonVm, eventBus, bootstrap, pendingVerbContribution) and INERT-DEFAULT cells (keep a typed closed default and name it: the share-verdict inputs, kahuProtected as "withhold all"). (b) ralias (open-node-vessel.ts +72, same cell regions: protectedMemo, boundWaiter, faceGrantRing, reverdictLater, protectedDocs, bootstrapTiddlers) and u1 (hunks at ~1694-1701, directly above the `let x!` block) both edit within a few lines; T10 must rebase on both. (c) A refusal on read turns the pre-makePool verb window (hazard C1) from an accidental TypeError into a named refusal, a visible behaviour change that a boot test must pin first. (d) Five hand guards become one cell kind: net deletion, but each guard returns `null` vs throws differently (3478/3499/3514 return null "memory-unavailable by name"; 1380/1402/3087 throw): a cell needs a try/peek form for the null-returning sites.
# Red-first: (i) per STAND cell, a unit red: `get` before `set` throws `CellUnset: vmManager` by name; control: after `set` it returns the value; set twice refuses (or is allowed only for declared multi-writer cells: activeAtom, selfSlotFedGate, representIfMoved, which need an explicit "widen" rule). (ii) Boot red (T6 pin): place `sync-wiki` on the verb registry between wireVerbs and makePool and expect the named refusal; control: after makePool it routes. (iii) Fail-closed control: with `kahuProtected` unset, a wire peer's ask for a Kahu-classed doc is withheld (red on today's code, which reads empty and withholds nothing). (iv) A mutant that moves `standSyncGates` before systemCanon must go red (pins F2's single-call-site invariant).
# VERDICT: NEEDS-RULING. Fork: do the share-verdict and guard nulls (antigenRing, edgeShadows, kahuProtected, selfSlotFedGate, siblingGate, nexusMembership, ownCarriageBoard, houseIslands) become refuse-on-read cells, or typed closed-default cells? Lean: two kinds. Refuse-by-name only for the seven STAND cells; closed-default for the verdict inputs, with the closed default being the DENY side (fix `kahuProtected`'s empty-map default to withhold-all-until-set, an old-shape cure in the same commit). Second fork: sequence T10 behind T6 AND behind both u1 and ralias (the road names only u1). T10 is CUT-READY for the seven STAND cells once T6 pins the order; the verdict-input cells ride with T11.

